fixture: 06-salvage-partial-draft
expectation: looks reasonable and is tested, but violates a criterion
violates: "Honest failure" (criterion 2 from context/review-criteria.md)
note:
  The PR reads as a UX win — real complaint, plausible fix, new test, warning still
  surfaced. It nonetheless turns an invalid model response into an `ok: true` draft
  with silently emptied sections, and the `schemaMismatch` report no longer fires on
  the repaired path, so the degradation is invisible in observability too. The
  summary backfill ("Draft summary unavailable.") is untranslated model-facing text
  reaching a pl/ru user, and `low_confidence` is reused for a different meaning than
  the prompt assigns it.
